      {
        "id": 224282,
        "name": "steveothemocker",
        "username": "steveothemocker",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/bc79bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-07T15:05:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would second the KMC Perfect Fit options. They are inexpensive, fit the sentinels cards really well, and aren't&nbsp;super thick so store in the collectors case without concern or having to shift dekcs to different drawers.&nbsp; I don't sleeve all my games but I will on any that sees regular play and we play Sentinels nearly every week.</p>\n<p>As far as just buying a new set, right now that is an option, but when I first got into SoTM, it was through trying the Steam Game to decide if I wanted to back OblivAeon. I really loved the game and wanted to play right away, but shopping around most place were sold out. The only place I could find any expansion was The TinkerPack (Patrick Rothfuss' charity driven webstore) to get Rook City/Infernal Relics box. So while right now its easy to get replacement sets that not always the case with the Ebbs and Flows of print runs.</p>\n<p>Plus if you're like me and end up playing&nbsp;probably too late into the night, so aren't very vigilante about putting everything up after the final game. It can be really frustrating to replace a whole game because your stupid feline companion decided to stick its head in an unfinished glass of water and ruin a handful of cards. Much nicer to just dry a table and some plastic.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
